g to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $0\\le x\\le 4,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{8}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{t}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ \\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2} \\\\ 16y & ={x}^{2} \\\\ x & =4\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.405,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.405}≈2.546$\n\n- For $y=0.824,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.824}≈3.631$\n\n- For $y=0.892,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.892}≈3.778$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ee473ff-8143-5b43-81e9-6dad15e3972f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ee473ff-8143-5b43-81e9-6dad15e3972f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee473ff-8143-5b43-81e9-6dad15e3972f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" "answer-6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" "answer-e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" "answer-653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" "answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" :answer/id #uuid "f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.902,\\,1.463,\\,1.683" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" :answer/id #uuid "6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.034,\\,1.736,\\,1.954" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" :answer/id #uuid "e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.478,\\,2.253,\\,2.564" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" :answer/id #uuid "653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.053,\\,2.894,\\,2.931" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe" :answer/id #uuid "d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.546,\\,3.631,\\,3.778" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b352c39a-e73c-5f2e-8ba3-a028566bd47b" :question/id #uuid "b352c39a-e73c-5f2e-8ba3-a028566bd47b" :question/math-academy-id "q-147776" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.041,\\,0.137,\\,0.782\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $x\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,{|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & \\,x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $x\\ge 1$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =1-y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{1-y} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.041,$ we get $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-0.041}}≈1.021$\n\n- For $y=0.137,$ we get $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-0.137}}≈1.076$\n\n- For $y=0.782,$ we get $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-0.782}}≈2.142$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4fe0e7e2-4434-5ec7-a990-869ba808178d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4fe0e7e2-4434-5ec7-a990-869ba808178d" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe0e7e2-4434-5ec7-a990-869ba808178d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a58b4639-5fe8-5f40-b735-09ec616d2904" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a58b4639-5fe8-5f40-b735-09ec616d2904" "answer-992bff68-e6f9-510c-a1a8-204e98c5f359" "answer-23f42d23-0ca4-550f-8e95-fa9e2bdb7998" "answer-856374f3-aa3c-55f9-8008-72655b2648e2" "answer-0559a1a5-e628-5eac-99b4-bf34a7beb20d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a58b4639-5fe8-5f40-b735-09ec616d2904" :answer/id #uuid "a58b4639-5fe8-5f40-b735-09ec616d2904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.021,\\,1.076,\\,2.142" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-992bff68-e6f9-510c-a1a8-204e98c5f359" :answer/id #uuid "992bff68-e6f9-510c-a1a8-204e98c5f359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.443,\\,2.564,\\,3.671" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23f42d23-0ca4-550f-8e95-fa9e2bdb7998" :answer/id #uuid "23f42d23-0ca4-550f-8e95-fa9e2bdb7998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.546,\\,1.699,\\,2.335" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856374f3-aa3c-55f9-8008-72655b2648e2" :answer/id #uuid "856374f3-aa3c-55f9-8008-72655b2648e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.940,\\,2.493,\\,3.058" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0559a1a5-e628-5eac-99b4-bf34a7beb20d" :answer/id #uuid "0559a1a5-e628-5eac-99b4-bf34a7beb20d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.633,\\,2.784,\\,3.093" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ef6d345-db21-5f3a-aad1-2b5e56cc5e56" :question/id #uuid "3ef6d345-db21-5f3a-aad1-2b5e56cc5e56" :question/math-academy-id "q-147698" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.209,\\,0.493,\\,0.826\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x},\\, & 1\\le x\\le e, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $1\\le x\\le e,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,1\\le x\\le e, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡x, & \\,1\\le x\\le e, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $1\\le x\\le e$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ x & ={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.209,$ we get $x={e}^{0.209}≈1.232$\n\n- For $y=0.493,$ we get $x={e}^{0.493}≈1.637$\n\n- For $y=0.826,$ we get $x={e}^{0.826}≈2.284$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6506b03f-ca93-59cf-b94c-6064957efb49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6506b03f-ca93-59cf-b94c-6064957efb49" :answer-field/id #uuid "6506b03f-ca93-59cf-b94c-6064957efb49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-632b77ae-b3d3-5a97-a7ad-12a184e6637d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-632b77ae-b3d3-5a97-a7ad-12a184e6637d" "answer-e0af9a98-12d1-5c58-8537-0b157b699025" "answer-9b3a9b79-41d8-5dd7-aa99-3bc9dc99d288" "answer-f7321105-ec7d-5b0e-b119-818ca4e002fa" "answer-ce6367be-6630-55f0-be18-4865fbd18d1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-632b77ae-b3d3-5a97-a7ad-12a184e6637d" :answer/id #uuid "632b77ae-b3d3-5a97-a7ad-12a184e6637d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.232,\\,1.637,\\,2.284" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0af9a98-12d1-5c58-8537-0b157b699025" :answer/id #uuid "e0af9a98-12d1-5c58-8537-0b157b699025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.343,\\,1.983,\\,2.487" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b3a9b79-41d8-5dd7-aa99-3bc9dc99d288" :answer/id #uuid "9b3a9b79-41d8-5dd7-aa99-3bc9dc99d288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.398,\\,1.793,\\,1.942" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7321105-ec7d-5b0e-b119-818ca4e002fa" :answer/id #uuid "f7321105-ec7d-5b0e-b119-818ca4e002fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.602,\\,1.834,\\,2.673" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce6367be-6630-55f0-be18-4865fbd18d1d" :answer/id #uuid "ce6367be-6630-55f0-be18-4865fbd18d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.920,\\,2.136,\\,2.536" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-483ad5dd-d09b-5c15-bb9e-2524c193114e" :question/id #uuid "483ad5dd-d09b-5c15-bb9e-2524c193114e" :question/math-academy-id "q-147745" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.691,\\,0.741,\\,0.839\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $0\\le x\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.691,$ we get $x=\\sqrt{0.691}≈0.831$\n\n- For $y=0.741,$ we get $x=\\sqrt{0.741}≈0.861$\n\n- For $y=0.839,$ we get $x=\\sqrt{0.839}≈0.916$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f547b9f3-9164-5013-b7a0-bea7e78cacbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f547b9f3-9164-5013-b7a0-bea7e78cacbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "f547b9f3-9164-5013-b7a0-bea7e78cacbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5ec97d5a-b5a2-539b-ab5d-c42e4fe5ae83" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84bf4099-962f-5056-8840-be25081e74c5" "answer-f6672f1f-cc34-5175-9f11-9cf409f90322" "answer-8b3874bc-e662-56d9-b74c-96550f2ac2f1" "answer-41ea1ddd-0512-515d-9f5d-135412757c8a" "answer-5ec97d5a-b5a2-539b-ab5d-c42e4fe5ae83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84bf4099-962f-5056-8840-be25081e74c5" :answer/id #uuid "84bf4099-962f-5056-8840-be25081e74c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.035,\\,0.351,\\,0.540" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6672f1f-cc34-5175-9f11-9cf409f90322" :answer/id #uuid "f6672f1f-cc34-5175-9f11-9cf409f90322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.353,\\,0.494,\\,0.631" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b3874bc-e662-56d9-b74c-96550f2ac2f1" :answer/id #uuid "8b3874bc-e662-56d9-b74c-96550f2ac2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.404,\\,0.646,\\,0.951" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ea1ddd-0512-515d-9f5d-135412757c8a" :answer/id #uuid "41ea1ddd-0512-515d-9f5d-135412757c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.503,\\,0.725,\\,0.837" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ec97d5a-b5a2-539b-ab5d-c42e4fe5ae83" :answer/id #uuid "5ec97d5a-b5a2-539b-ab5d-c42e4fe5ae83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.831,\\,0.861,\\,0.916" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189408 :tutorial/content "Most statistical computer packages have functionality that allows data from a particular probability distribution to be simulated. In this lesson, we'll learn how this process works.\n\nFor example, suppose we have a random variable with the cumulative distribution function \n\n$$\nF(x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+e^{-x}}\\,, \\qquad x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=F(x)$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/f2/f26b4b7871d1f2b4c7a983986f596c4b599d24fbf34c87b443fb21025f26b5ad.png)\n\n \n\nSuppose we want to generate a sample of size $n=3$ from this distribution. To do this, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, draw a random sample of size $n=3$ from the uniform distribution $Y \\sim U[0,1].$\n\n- Then, find the values $x_i$ such that $y_i=F(x_i).$ In other words, \n\n$$\nx_i=F^{-1}(y_i), \\qquad i=1,2,3.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x)$ is strictly increasing and therefore $F^{-1}(y)$ exists for all $y\\in (0,1).$ \n\nSuppose that we run our simulation and generate $n=3$ numbers from $Y\\sim U[0,1],$ and that our three numbers (rounded to $3$ decimal places) are \n\n$$\ny_1 = 0.214, \\qquad y_2 = 0.707, \\qquad y_3 = 0.819.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe'll now use this data to generate three numbers $x_1, x_2,$ and $x_3$ drawn from the distribution with CDF $F(x).$ The three $x_i$'s are the numbers shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d9/d93db6abed9b1f227e5badb0d71868b1aee261d803af929e1fd8e45dc5f2932b.png)\n\nTo compute our $x_i$'s, we first need to find the inverse of $F(x).$ So we first write $y=F(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ {e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1}{y}-1 \\\\ {e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1-y}{y} \\\\ -x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y}) \\\\ x & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{1-y}{y})}^{-1} \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{1-y}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 < y < 1.$\n\nFinally, substituting the values $y_1,y_2,y_3$ into the formula for $x=F^{-1}(y),$ we obtain \n\n$$\nx_1 \\approx -1.301, \\qquad x_2 \\approx 0.881, \\qquad x_3 \\approx 1.510.\n$$\n\nThe algorithm above can be formalized in the following theorem:\n\n*Let the random variable $Y \\sim U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a) = 0, F(b) = 1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a \\lt x \\lt b,$ where $a$ and $b$ could be infinite. Then, the random variable $X,$ given by \n\n$$\nX = F^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\n is a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$*" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188461 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186188056 :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.352, \\quad 0.567, \\quad 0.801\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n![](images/2c/2c4ac4b0cf243ba8b49024132642a3856210daa5a603ed534e636caef0083629.svg)\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] [17592186188056 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y \\sim U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a) = 0, F(b) = 1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a <            x <            b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX = F^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y = F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $1 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\lt y \\lt 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ 2-y & =\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y = 0.352,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.352} \\approx 1.214$\n\n- For $y = 0.567,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.567} \\approx 1.396$\n\n- For $y = 0.801,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.801} \\approx 1.668$"] [17592186188060 :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.354, \\quad 0.593, \\quad 0.792\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n![](images/ea/ea0ee4d1fcf2e423ebd438e784160e525cb2486e91ba833cd84aae9ff0568344.svg)\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] [17592186188060 :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y \\sim U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a) = 0, F(b) = 1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a <            x <            b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX = F^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ we have\n![](images/53/535220c76d363aac546f42314de13394c1fd8b3001e95028a4215867ebc6ed41.svg)\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n![](images/8e/8eef1c7b3d8a69137cf7ac23ecf721751f43449d48b6f450256e15f501ee4c91.svg)\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y = F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ and $0 \\lt y \\lt 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y = 0.354,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.354) \\approx 0.362$\n\n- For $y = 0.593,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.593) \\approx 0.635$\n\n- For $y = 0.792,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.792) \\approx 0.914$"] ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/id #uuid "be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1"] ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-147598"] ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.112,\\,0.455,\\,0.800\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}, & \\,x\\le 0, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $x\\le 0$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{x} \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.112,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.112)≈-2.189$\n\n- For $y=0.455,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.455)≈-0.787$\n\n- For $y=0.800,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.800)≈-0.223$"] ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-e896c598-93c0-535b-bc5e-efc7006916d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e896c598-93c0-535b-bc5e-efc7006916d9"] ["answer-78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" :answer/id #uuid "78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311"] ["answer-78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" :answer/value "-1.768,\\,-0.773,\\,-0.231"] ["answer-e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" :answer/id #uuid "e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b"] ["answer-e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" :answer/value "-1.998,\\,-1.067,\\,-0.554"] ["answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer/id #uuid "8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420"] ["answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer/value "-2.189,\\,-0.787,\\,-0.223"] ["answer-49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" :answer/id #uuid "49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4"] ["answer-49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" :answer/value "-2.657,\\,-2.134,\\,-2.002"] ["answer-30c8a159-2ab7-583f-b9ca-e09e33a5305f" :answer/id 