ecimal places."] ["question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.257,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.257}≈0.636$\n\n- For $y=0.498,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.498}≈0.793$\n\n- For $y=0.632,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.632}≈0.858$"] ["question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80"] ["answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" :answer/id #uuid "942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967"] ["answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" :answer/value "0.221,\\,0.467,\\,0.668"] ["answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" :answer/id #uuid "e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324"] ["answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" :answer/value "0.281,\\,0.546,\\,0.771"] ["answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" :answer/id #uuid "8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0"] ["answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" :answer/value "0.467,\\,0.623,\\,0.845"] ["answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" :answer/id #uuid "6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18"] ["answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" :answer/value "0.502,\\,0.798,\\,0.904"] ["answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer/id #uuid "88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc"] ["answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer/value "0.636,\\,0.793,\\,0.858"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/correct "answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/choices "answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/choices "answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/choices "answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18"] ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/choices "answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc"] ["question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80"] [17592186188348 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671"] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/id #uuid "d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7"] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-147600"] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.459,\\,0.714,\\,0.938\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve for the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le y\\le 1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}} \\\\ 1+{e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ {e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1-y}{y} \\\\ -x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y}) \\\\ x & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.459,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.459}{0.459})≈-0.164$\n\n- For $y=0.714,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.714}{0.714})≈0.915$\n\n- For $y=0.938,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.938}{0.938})≈2.717$"] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577"] ["answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer/id #uuid "2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d"] ["answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer/value "-0.164,\\,0.915,\\,2.717"] ["answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" :answer/id #uuid "d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d"] ["answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" :answer/value "-0.802,\\,-0.456,\\,1.034"] ["answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" :answer/id #uuid "c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007"] ["answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" :answer/value "-2.203,\\,-1.754,\\,0.650"] ["answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8" :answer/id #uuid "508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8"] ["answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8" :answer/value "-3.983,\\,-2.021,\\,-1.673"] ["answer-88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221" :answer/id #uuid "88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221"] ["answer-88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221" :answer/value "0.105,\\,0.876,\\,1.392"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/correct "answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/choices "answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/choices "answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/choices "answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/choices "answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8"] ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/choices "answer-88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221"] ["question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577"] [17592186188348 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/id #uuid "f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/math-academy-id "q-147602"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.256,\\,0.783,\\,0.809\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<-1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}(x+1), & \\,-1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $-1\\le x\\le 3$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+1) \\\\ 4y & =x+1 \\\\ x & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.256,$ we get $x=4(0.256)-1=0.024$\n\n- For $y=0.783,$ we get $x=4(0.783)-1=2.132$\n\n- For $y=0.809,$ we get $x=4(0.809)-1=2.236$"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/id #uuid "73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046"] ["answer-d7429141-e258-5710-aeba-2d59c02dfe22" :answer/id #uuid "d7429141-e258-5710-aeba-2d59c02dfe22"] ["answer-d7429141-e258-5710-aeba-2d59c02dfe22" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d7429141-e258-5710-aeba-2d59c02dfe22" :answer/value "-0.134,\\,1.672,\\,2.237"] ["answer-f562c9bf-0f21-562e-89ac-ab5a3185530b" :answer/id #uuid "f562c9bf-0f21-562e-89ac-ab5a3185530b"] ["answer-f562c9bf-0f21-562e-89ac-ab5a3185530b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f562c9bf-0f21-562e-89ac-ab5a3185530b" :answer/value "-0.564,\\,0.045,\\,1.045"] ["answer-649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06" :answer/id #uuid "649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06"] ["answer-649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06" :answer/value "0.024,\\,2.132,\\,2.236"] ["answer-6be10170-2653-5422-a7c0-a9ed69479d92" :answer/id #uuid "6be10170-2653-5422-a7c0-a9ed69479d92"] ["answer-6be10170-2653-5422-a7c0-a9ed69479d92" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6be10170-2653-5422-a7c0-a9ed69479d92" :answer/value "1.123,\\,2.345,\\,2.934"] ["answer-1dd7dba3-7e69-5bcf-826b-cc2958b6fd98" :answer/id #uuid "1dd7dba3-7e69-5bcf-826b-cc2958b6fd98"] ["answer-1dd7dba3-7e69-5bcf-826b-cc2958b6fd98" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1dd7dba3-7e69-5bcf-826b-cc2958b6fd98" :answer/value "1.203,\\,1.879,\\,2.845"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/correct "answer-649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/choices "answer-d7429141-e258-5710-aeba-2d59c02dfe22"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/choices "answer-f562c9bf-0f21-562e-89ac-ab5a3185530b"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/choices "answer-649c7229-aa22-5421-af0c-17563057ef06"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/choices "answer-6be10170-2653-5422-a7c0-a9ed69479d92"] ["answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046" :answer-field/choices "answer-1dd7dba3-7e69-5bcf-826b-cc2958b6fd98"] ["question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-73caafd6-d60a-5362-be7d-d1d46896b046"] [17592186188348 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788"] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/id #uuid "4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea"] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-147601"] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.321,\\,0.567,\\,0.804\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({e}^{x}),\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le y\\le 1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{y\\pi }{2} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({e}^{x}) \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{y\\pi }{2}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{y\\pi }{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.321,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{0.321\\pi }{2}))≈-0.595$\n\n- For $y=0.567,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{0.567\\pi }{2}))≈0.212$\n\n- For $y=0.804,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{0.804\\pi }{2}))≈1.146$"] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e"] ["answer-00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9" :answer/id #uuid "00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9"] ["answer-00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9" :answer/value "-0.595,\\,0.212,\\,1.146"] ["answer-5992f636-bbef-5d92-8070-1748eaa01d5a" :answer/id #uuid "5992f636-bbef-5d92-8070-1748eaa01d5a"] ["answer-5992f636-bbef-5d92-8070-1748eaa01d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5992f636-bbef-5d92-8070-1748eaa01d5a" :answer/value "-1.093,\\,-0.442,\\,0.856"] ["answer-db138c8d-b21c-5164-89b9-248159a62bb6" :answer/id #uuid "db138c8d-b21c-5164-89b9-248159a62bb6"] ["answer-db138c8d-b21c-5164-89b9-248159a62bb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-db138c8d-b21c-5164-89b9-248159a62bb6" :answer/value "-2.156,\\,-1.045,\\,-0.504"] ["answer-dd78e176-69d9-5cad-a0f6-feffa2678056" :answer/id #uuid "dd78e176-69d9-5cad-a0f6-feffa2678056"] ["answer-dd78e176-69d9-5cad-a0f6-feffa2678056" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dd78e176-69d9-5cad-a0f6-feffa2678056" :answer/value "0.431,\\,1.984,\\,2.598"] ["answer-68357845-bce6-554e-84b7-a271aaeb70aa" :answer/id #uuid "68357845-bce6-554e-84b7-a271aaeb70aa"] ["answer-68357845-bce6-554e-84b7-a271aaeb70aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-68357845-bce6-554e-84b7-a271aaeb70aa" :answer/value "1.372,\\,1.804,\\,2.765"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/correct "answer-00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/choices "answer-00c374ab-6913-5cd0-a99e-c528c2de09a9"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/choices "answer-5992f636-bbef-5d92-8070-1748eaa01d5a"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/choices "answer-db138c8d-b21c-5164-89b9-248159a62bb6"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/choices "answer-dd78e176-69d9-5cad-a0f6-feffa2678056"] ["answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e" :answer-field/choices "answer-68357845-bce6-554e-84b7-a271aaeb70aa"] ["question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b9cabec7-d001-59f7-b4e5-a424a8d1286e"] [17592186188348 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea"] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/id #uuid "67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9"] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-147778"] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.198,\\,0.266,\\,0.322\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,{|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =2(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<1, \\\\ 2(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}), & \\,1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $1\\le x\\le 4$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} & =1-\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{2-y}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x} & =\\frac{2}{2-y} \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{(2-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.198,$ we get $x=\\frac{4}{(2-0.198)^{2}}≈1.232$\n\n- For $y=0.266,$ we get $x=\\frac{4}{(2-0.266)^{2}}≈1.330$\n\n- For $y=0.322,$ we get $x=\\frac{4}{(2-0.322)^{2}}≈1.421$"] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7"] ["answer-d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a" :answer/id #uuid "d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a"] ["answer-d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a" :answer/value "1.232,\\,1.330,\\,1.421"] ["answer-ad6dcec7-cb37-5574-bdae-e38c0d88cc3e" :answer/id #uuid "ad6dcec7-cb37-5574-bdae-e38c0d88cc3e"] ["answer-ad6dcec7-cb37-5574-bdae-e38c0d88cc3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ad6dcec7-cb37-5574-bdae-e38c0d88cc3e" :answer/value "1.745,\\,2.323,\\,2.987"] ["answer-1ed81a42-4f5b-592d-9877-e155aa0820d4" :answer/id #uuid "1ed81a42-4f5b-592d-9877-e155aa0820d4"] ["answer-1ed81a42-4f5b-592d-9877-e155aa0820d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1ed81a42-4f5b-592d-9877-e155aa0820d4" :answer/value "1.791,\\,1.831,\\,1.983"] ["answer-d695e024-941b-5f2c-8ffd-481b7c531017" :answer/id #uuid "d695e024-941b-5f2c-8ffd-481b7c531017"] ["answer-d695e024-941b-5f2c-8ffd-481b7c531017" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d695e024-941b-5f2c-8ffd-481b7c531017" :answer/value "2.029,\\,2.322,\\,2.799"] ["answer-eb00bf92-1637-5fdb-aea4-e09fbcb06285" :answer/id #uuid "eb00bf92-1637-5fdb-aea4-e09fbcb06285"] ["answer-eb00bf92-1637-5fdb-aea4-e09fbcb06285" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eb00bf92-1637-5fdb-aea4-e09fbcb06285" :answer/value "2.543,\\,2.806,\\,3.281"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/correct "answer-d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/choices "answer-d78d7fa8-dcf4-5bb1-99c1-d0866aa1f60a"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/choices "answer-ad6dcec7-cb37-5574-bdae-e38c0d88cc3e"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/choices "answer-1ed81a42-4f5b-592d-9877-e155aa0820d4"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/choices "answer-d695e024-941b-5f2c-8ffd-481b7c531017"] ["answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7" :answer-field/choices "answer-eb00bf92-1637-5fdb-aea4-e09fbcb06285"] ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4ec6b574-4380-5af5-a64d-c3a6fdb29ec7"] [17592186188352 :knowledge-point/questions "question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9"] ["question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" :question/id #uuid "58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b"] ["question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" :question/math-academy-id "q-147752"] ["question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.405,\\,0.824,\\,0.892\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places."] ["question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $0\\le x\\le 4,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & \\,0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{8}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{t}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ \\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2} \\\\ 16y & ={x}^{2} \\\\ x & =4\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.405,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.405}≈2.546$\n\n- For $y=0.824,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.824}≈3.631$\n\n- For $y=0.892,$ we get $x=4\\sqrt{0.892}≈3.778$"] ["question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-1ee473ff-8143-5b43-81e9-6dad15e3972f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee473ff-8143-5b43-81e9-6dad15e3972f"] ["answer-f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" :answer/id #uuid "f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7"] ["answer-f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f41ac435-1c3a-57c0-b25f-beb895ca90b7" :answer/value "0.902,\\,1.463,\\,1.683"] ["answer-6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" :answer/id #uuid "6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b"] ["answer-6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6567f6f8-c441-5894-846d-a5e89207da3b" :answer/value "1.034,\\,1.736,\\,1.954"] ["answer-e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" :answer/id #uuid "e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693"] ["answer-e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e13b7ccf-e151-5505-959f-cc939906e693" :answer/value "1.478,\\,2.253,\\,2.564"] ["answer-653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" :answer/id #uuid "653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c"] ["answer-653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-653df948-6dc8-5e58-977c-49f0d870e61c" :answer/value "2.053,\\,2.894,\\,2.931"] ["answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe" :answer/id #uuid "d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe"] ["answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c07eeb313fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d69c6365-efc5-554a-ac72-1c0